# Unity C# Code Style Rules

## NO COMMENTS POLICY
- NEVER generate comments of any type (no //, no /* */, no ///, no XML docs)
- Code must be self-documenting through clear naming
- Use descriptive variable, method, and class names instead of comments
- The only exception: #region names

## NO DOCUMENTATION FILES
- NEVER create README.md, CHANGELOG.md, or any .md files
- NEVER create documentation files of any type
- NEVER create .txt documentation files
- Code is the only documentation needed

## REGION GROUPING
- Group related functions using #region/#endregion
- Region names should be descriptive and use Title Case
- Examples: "Networking Config", "Event Handlers", "Initialization", "Public API"

```csharp
#region Networking Config

public void SetupConnection() { }
public void ConfigureTimeout() { }
public void SetRetryPolicy() { }

#endregion

#region Event Handlers

private void OnPlayerJoined() { }
private void OnPlayerLeft() { }

#endregion
```

## ALWAYS
1. NO COMMENTS - code must be self-documenting
2. Use #region to group related functions
3. Use descriptive names for variables, methods, classes
4. Follow naming conventions: SDB_, ref_, Util_ prefixes

## NEVER
1. Generate comments of any kind (no //, /*, ///, XML docs)
2. Create README.md, CHANGELOG.md, or any documentation files
3. Create .md or .txt documentation files
4. Use vague or abbreviated names
5. Leave code without proper region grouping
